WebGPU capability
-----------------

Copyright (c) 2026 cppctamber / CarbonEngineJS contributors

The WebGPU device, descriptor, resource, pipeline, binding, and draw
realization under `src/engine/webgpu` is original CarbonEngineJS work. The
adjacent-batch grouping behavior in `core/batchGroups.js` adapts the documented
CarbonEngine `Tr2RenderContextBase::RenderBatchGroup` and `CanBeBinned`
semantics; its exact source paths and deliberate WebGPU deviations are recorded
in that file.

The repository-only WebGPU verification harness uses Microsoft Playwright as a
development dependency. Playwright is licensed under the Apache License 2.0;
it is not a runtime dependency and no Playwright source or browser binary is
redistributed in this package. No acquired GPU packages, effect bytes,
geometry, textures, or other game assets are included.

Resource capability
-------------------

The resource capability owns resource lifecycle, format selection, canonical
GPU-free shader/reflection models, and the format readers under
`src/resource/formats`. Copied format implementations retain their original
license and notice files under `format-notices/<format>/`, including notices
for meshoptimizer, yaml, black-reader-js, and bundled Wwise codebook data.

The bundled Black definition JSON is a generated CarbonEngineJS schema artifact
copied from `format-carbon` revision
`d2a3c67cf3d46e8ba78ca19e66558d868178ec24`. Its digest and retention purpose
are recorded in `docs/resource/formats/provenance.md`; it contains no game asset.

The GR2/GSF reader was migrated after its EUPL-derived decoder was replaced by
a validated clean-room implementation and the donor was relicensed MIT. The
modern cFSD decoder and reviewed dataset schemas decode caller-supplied bytes
and include no acquired game data, decoded tables, or native loader modules.

